  "text": "[patient] Hi my name is leah, i just give birth last july 1, and i had develop a rash from one of the antibiotics that they gave for my epidoral.... i had a rashes around my tommy they gave me a benadril prescription from the hospital. The rash is gone on my tommy but i had another rashes again all over my body now its redesh and super itchy what can i do with this?\n[doctor] Hello,Thanks for the query.You have developed a drug allergy.Keep taking benadryl, this will help in controlling itch.For the rash you can apply a mild steroid cream.Mild steroids can be used during breast feeding, so dont worry regarding that.Let me know if you have any other doubt.you can ask a direct question to me on this forum, following the below link.https://urldefense.com/v3/__http://www.healthcaremagic.com/doctors/dr-rahul-kumar/64818Wishing__;!!Mih3wA!SBzm6_kI6hCZ58EPH6N_05MFfiPbxWXT0a2TJCdFQObRWm5mV5ur7hUOMa8clQ$  you a good health.Thank you",
